[ceiling] This is the rear shoulder of the donor-body cavity at Z39, around the soda passage and forward of the flavor opening. The shoulder follows the metal body's plateau envelope. It is inclined 15 degrees to the bed in the base's -15 degree print pose. The donor cavity is open below for inspection and support cleanup before installing the metal body; removal effort and contact finish are physical print observations.
